WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:16.209
In this video, we are going to introduce you
with one of the most plausible theories out

00:00:16.209 --> 00:00:18.340
there,
in which fierce Lyanna Mormont who killed

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:22.470
a giant at the age of 13, becoming a gianstbane
herself,

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:26.500
was the daughter of none other than Tormund
Giantsbane who also slew a giant at the age

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:27.770
of 10.

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:29.230
Like father, like daughter...

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:32.680
Lyanna's mother, Maege Mormont, the she-bear
was the lady of Bear Island

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:34.780
and the head of House Mormont.

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:39.640
In the books, she has many daughters and in
the show, she had only one, Lyanna, namesake

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:42.430
of Lyanna Stark, Lord Eddard Stark's sister(sibling).

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:46.300
There are indications that Maege Mormont had
an affair with Tormund

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:49.270
and it resulted with a great warrior, Lyanna
Mormont.

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:53.750
The sigil of House Mormont is a bear surrounded
by white with green borders.

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:58.600
Just like Lyanna Stark was called the she-wolf
due to the wolf being the sigil of her house,

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:01.370
Maege Mormont was known in the North as the
she-bear.

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:03.769
Tormund boasts of having bedded a she-bear.

00:01:03.769 --> 00:01:07.750
There's a scene on the show when Tormund explains
how he came by this name.

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:12.119
In the mentioned scene, Tormund boasts to
Jon Snow that he once accidentally seduced

00:01:12.119 --> 00:01:17.970
a bear during an intense snowstorm, believing
she was merely a stout, hot-tempered woman,

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:21.540
which funny enough is exactly how Maege Mormont
is described in the books.

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:26.430
When Tormund awoke, he was badly scratched
and there was a ''she-bear pelt'' lying on

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:27.430
the ground.

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:32.250
In addition to all these clues, no one knows
who the father of Lyanna is or even if Maege

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:33.250
ever married.

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:37.400
Nonetheless, all of Maege's daughters
and on the show her only daughter Lyanna carry

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:41.810
the surname Mormont
and none appear to be considered bastards.

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:46.440
It's possible that Maege's husband came from
a family of a lower nobility than the Mormonts

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:51.800
or no nobility at all, in which case a woman
can prefer to retain her own surname for herself

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:53.400
and for her children.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:56.760
One of many of Tormund's nicknames is Husband
to Bears.

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:01.400
In the books, Maege's other daughter, Alysane,
smilingly shares the rumor claiming that Mormont

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:05.380
women are skinchangers
who turn into bears and find mates in the

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:06.380
woods.

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:09.970
In fact, Alysane claims her two children are
fathered by bears.

00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:14.650
One of the titles of Tormund Giantsbane is
Father To Bears,

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:17.629
meaning that some of the Mormonts may have
wilding blood.

00:02:17.629 --> 00:02:21.069
On the gate of Mormont's hall is a carving
of a woman in a bearskin

00:02:21.069 --> 00:02:25.959
with a child in one arm suckling at her breast
and a battleaxe in the other.

00:02:25.959 --> 00:02:30.019
It's also mentioned that women of House Mormont
learned how to defend themselves from wildlings

00:02:30.019 --> 00:02:34.599
who avoided the Wall entirely by using boats
to cross the bay from the Froyen Shore on

00:02:34.599 --> 00:02:35.860
the other side.

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:38.909
So we know the wildlings were sometimes raiding
their lands.

00:02:38.909 --> 00:02:42.340
Perhaps that's how Maege and Tormund met and
fell in love,

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:45.620
and the byproduct of that love may have been
Lyanna Mormont.

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:49.650
The show didn't confirm this, in my opinion
probably the most plausible theory in the

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:53.579
Game of Thrones realm, but there's still hope
for the books to do the deed

00:02:53.579 --> 00:02:58.260
and hopefully, Lyanna survives the fight against
the giant in the books, just like Tormund

00:02:58.260 --> 00:02:59.260
did.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:02.450
On the bright side of the show version, at
least House Mormont and all of its members

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:07.690
did not suffer the same fate as all other
characters, which is being butchered by season

00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:08.690
8.

00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:13.019
Ironically they were slain, but not by writing,
but by their bravery and loyalty.

00:03:13.019 --> 00:03:17.969
Here they stand, true to their words, both
Jorah and Lyanna stood their ground defending

00:03:17.969 --> 00:03:18.969
Winterfell.

00:03:18.969 --> 00:03:22.280
In conclusion, there's a high possibility
that Lyanna Mormont was on the show

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:25.590
and still is in the books the daughter of
Tormund Giantsbane,

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:30.230
the Husband to Bears and the Father to Bears
and the she-bear he bedded was none other

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:32.269
than the she-bear Maege Mormont.

00:03:32.269 --> 00:03:33.900
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:37.639
I hope you enjoyed this video and if you did
please give it a big thumbs up and I hope

00:03:37.639 --> 00:03:40.909
to see you in the next one!

00:03:40.909 --> 00:03:43.499
Peace

